  "rationale": "I found no gaps. I read the cited sources and the neighbouring `requirements.ci.span`, but did not run the tests.\n\n**Obligations**\n1. The `requirement` string in each evidence file MUST match all Markdown inside its fenced `{req}` directive, excluding leading and trailing whitespace.\n2. Habeas MUST report changed requirement text.\n\n**Code for obligation 1**\n- `collect_definitions` in `src/evidence.rs` builds the expected text. It takes the body between the fences, drops the option lines with `without_options`, then calls `.trim()`.\n  - That body span covers headings, nested fences and blank lines.\n  - `without_options` in `src/lib.rs` carries an `{impl}` of this requirement.\n  - The trimming line in `collect_definitions` is marked `{impl}` for `requirements.ci.span`. That requirement's text says the body is all Markdown between the fence lines and that leading and trailing whitespace are excluded when comparing with evidence. I treat this as correctly marked.\n- The comparison is in `validate_evidence_file` (`src/evidence.rs`, `{impl}` of `requirements.ci.requirement_text`). It checks `text != expected.text` for the `requirement` field, or `example` for examples.\n\n**Code for obligation 2**\n- When the strings differ, `validate_evidence_file` pushes the error `\"{label}: requirement text changed (source)\"` with a `compact_diff`.\n- The `requirement must not be empty` check is not named in this text, but it falls within the evidence-validation behaviour the same function implements for `requirements.ci.schema`.\n\n**Tests**\n- `validates_full_names_requirement_text_and_input_lines` (`src/evidence.rs`) has a directive body with a blank line and a nested code fence.\n  - The evidence string matches the body exactly, minus the trailing newline, and validation reports no errors.\n  - This covers matching all Markdown and the whitespace trimming.\n- `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` checks that \"requirement text changed\" and the diff lines `- Old text.` and `+ First.` are reported. This covers reporting changed text.\n- `anchored_files_must_be_completely_covered_and_resolvable` shows option lines are excluded from the compared text, using `without_options`. It asserts there is no \"text changed\" error.\n\nBoth obligations have code with `{impl}` references and tests with `{test}` references. I found no unmarked implementing code and no unspecified behaviour.",
